# The two ATLAS binary degree-220 matrix pairs

The four literal matrices come from the ATLAS files `M24G1-f2r220aB0.m1`,
`.m2`, `M24G1-f2r220bB0.m1`, `.m2`. Bit j of stored row i is source entry
(i,j), with both indices starting at zero. The exported matrices are the
transposes of the source row-action matrices, for use with column vectors.

These are matrix data, not representations of M₂₄ or irreducibility claims.
`source/generate.py` reproduces the transcription and checks the recorded
source hashes. The source files and attribution are retained in `source/`.
The mathematical certificates are checked separately in Lean.

Source: ATLAS of Finite Group Representations, R. A. Wilson, S. J. Nickerson
and J. N. Bray, https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/spor/M24/.
-/

